1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,261
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,261 --> 00:00:04,303
In this lesson, we'll build
a pipeline from scratch.

3
00:00:04,303 --> 00:00:07,990
You'll create it, name its stages,
put them in the right order,

4
00:00:07,990 --> 00:00:11,618
and learn how to change it later
without losing a single deal.

5
00:00:12,518 --> 00:00:17,288
Before you click anything, write down the
steps a customer goes through with you.

6
00:00:17,288 --> 00:00:21,882
Make each stage something that has already
happened, like consultation booked.

7
00:00:21,882 --> 00:00:25,828
That way, anyone on the team can
tell exactly where a deal belongs.

8
00:00:25,828 --> 00:00:29,950
For implants, that might be: new
lead, contacted, consultation booked,

9
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:33,307
treatment plan sent, deposit
paid, and treatment started.

10
00:00:34,157 --> 00:00:37,823
Pipelines live in their own
tab, next to Opportunities.

11
00:00:37,823 --> 00:00:41,223
Each row shows a pipeline
and its stages, in order.

12
00:00:41,223 --> 00:00:46,422
This account already has three: patient
journey, Invisalign, and reactivation.

13
00:00:47,273 --> 00:00:51,952
Let's build one for dental implants, which
have a longer journey than a check-up.

14
00:00:51,952 --> 00:00:54,955
Click Create new pipeline,
and give it a clear name.

15
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:58,903
Kyntlo starts you off
with three example stages.

16
00:00:58,903 --> 00:01:01,097
Click any stage name to change it.

17
00:01:01,097 --> 00:01:03,872
I'll rename Booked, to
Consultation Booked.

18
00:01:04,721 --> 00:01:07,873
Now click Add stage for
each step that follows.

19
00:01:07,873 --> 00:01:08,745
Deposit paid.

20
00:01:08,745 --> 00:01:09,952
Treatment started.

21
00:01:09,952 --> 00:01:11,561
And treatment plan sent.

22
00:01:12,377 --> 00:01:12,689
Oops!

23
00:01:12,689 --> 00:01:15,874
Treatment plan sent should
come before the deposit.

24
00:01:15,874 --> 00:01:16,561
No problem.

25
00:01:16,561 --> 00:01:20,371
Grab it by the handle on the
left, and drag it up into place.

26
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:23,805
Deals always move from the
top stage to the bottom one.

27
00:01:24,656 --> 00:01:29,583
The two switches on each stage decide
whether it appears in your dashboard's funnel

28
00:01:29,583 --> 00:01:30,770
chart and pie chart.

29
00:01:30,770 --> 00:01:32,076
Leave them on for now.

30
00:01:32,076 --> 00:01:36,765
You might switch one off later, if a
stage clutters a chart without telling you

31
00:01:36,765 --> 00:01:37,300
anything.

32
00:01:38,150 --> 00:01:40,105
When you're happy, click Create.

33
00:01:40,105 --> 00:01:44,258
The new pipeline appears in your
list, with all six stages in order.

34
00:01:44,258 --> 00:01:48,533
Its open value is zero for now,
because it doesn't have any deals yet.

35
00:01:49,383 --> 00:01:53,191
Back on the Opportunities tab,
pick it from the pipeline menu.

36
00:01:53,191 --> 00:01:56,938
There's your new board, with
one empty column for each stage,

37
00:01:56,938 --> 00:01:58,474
ready for its first deal.

38
00:01:58,474 --> 00:02:02,897
From now on, whenever you add an
opportunity, or a workflow creates one,

39
00:02:02,897 --> 00:02:05,538
you can choose this
pipeline and its stage.

40
00:02:06,388 --> 00:02:08,828
You can change a pipeline at any time.

41
00:02:08,828 --> 00:02:12,745
Click the pencil next to it to
rename, reorder or add stages.

42
00:02:12,745 --> 00:02:16,854
Existing deals stay in their
stages, even when you reorder them.

43
00:02:16,854 --> 00:02:20,193
Just move deals out of a
stage before you delete it.

44
00:02:21,042 --> 00:02:24,758
One thing to check: the Starter
plan includes one pipeline,

45
00:02:24,758 --> 00:02:27,843
so shape that one around
your main sales process.

46
00:02:27,843 --> 00:02:31,055
Growth gives you up to
three, and Pro is unlimited.

47
00:02:31,905 --> 00:02:33,053
Here's a pro tip.

48
00:02:33,053 --> 00:02:35,012
Aim for five to seven stages.

49
00:02:35,012 --> 00:02:38,186
Fewer, and you can't see
where deals get stuck.

50
00:02:38,186 --> 00:02:43,048
More, and your team will stop moving
cards, because it feels like admin.

51
00:02:43,048 --> 00:02:44,804
Simple pipelines get used.

52
00:02:45,672 --> 00:02:47,126
Your pipeline is ready!

53
00:02:47,126 --> 00:02:51,993
In the next lesson, we'll work the board
day to day: moving deals, filtering,

54
00:02:51,993 --> 00:02:54,205
and making changes to many at once.

55
00:02:54,205 --> 00:02:55,089
See you there.
